Angry Birds Classic 8.0.3 → arm64 port
======================================

THE PORT (original work in this repository)
-------------------------------------------
The ARM32→ARM64 emulation shim (port/shim/), the reproducible build pipeline
(port/build_apk.sh, port/docker/, port/reproduce.sh), the de-phone-home tooling
(port/depermission.py, port/manifest_firebase_off.py), and all other original
source code and documentation here are:

    Copyright (c) 2026 Ronen Zyroff <rzyroff@gmail.com>
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 (see LICENSE).

GPLv2 applies because the shim statically links the Unicorn Engine (GPLv2), so the
built shim binary is a combined GPLv2 work. The complete corresponding source is
this repository, and the reproducible build regenerates the binary byte-for-byte.

THE GAME (bundled, unmodified third-party content)
--------------------------------------------------
"Angry Birds", "Angry Birds Classic", the game itself, and all of its native
engine code, Java code (classes.dex), assets, and artwork — as bundled here in
apks/com.rovio.angrybirds@8.0.3.apk.xz and reproduced inside the output APK — are:

    Copyright (c) Rovio Entertainment Corporation. All rights reserved.

They are included here UNMODIFIED, for personal archival and interoperability
(running a legitimately-owned copy of a delisted game on hardware whose CPU can
no longer execute its original 32-bit ARM code). The port neither modifies the
game's code/assets nor circumvents any technical protection measure on them; it
adds an emulation layer so the unaltered engine can run on an AArch64-only CPU,
and neutralizes the app's network permissions.

This project is NOT affiliated with, authorized by, sponsored by, or endorsed by
Rovio Entertainment Corporation. "Angry Birds" and related marks are trademarks
of Rovio Entertainment Corporation.

THIRD-PARTY TOOLING
-------------------
The build fetches, at image-build time, the Android NDK (Google) and the Unicorn
Engine (https://www.unicorn-engine.org/, GPLv2), each under its own license.
Unicorn is statically linked into the shim; see its license for the terms that
implies for redistribution of the built shim binary.
